  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Earth Day is celebrated annually on April 22 to promote environmental protection, with the first event occurring in 1970. It is the world's largest civic event, engaging over a billion people in actions like planting trees, reducing plastic, and protesting pollution. The 2025 theme focuses on \"Our Power, Our Planet,\" advocating for a rapid shift to renewable energy.Key Aspects of Earth Day:Purpose: To raise awareness of environmental issues like climate change, deforestation, and pollution.History: Founded in 1970 by U.S. Senator Gaylord Nelson after an oil spill in Santa Barbara, it mobilized 20 million people, launching the modern environmental movement.Theme (2025/2026): Focuses on transitioning to renewable energy, specifically urging a tripling of global renewable energy generation by 2030.How to Take Action (Earth Day Activities):Reduce, Reuse, Recycle: Focus on reducing single-use plastic consumption.Plant Trees/Gardens: Create habitats for animals and improve air quality.Participate in Cleanup Events: Clean up local parks, beaches, and neighborhoods.Support Renewable Energy: Advocate for solar and wind energy in your community.You can find local events and actions on the official EARTHDAY.ORG website.",
